# Read Russian in 14 letters
subtitle: "Fourteen Cyrillic letters, a handful of words and a short Russian text you can read by the end, learned the way memory works best."
teaches: ["reading/cyrillic-letters"]
thumb: "band \"PECTOPAH? Read it again.\" stamp \"RESTORAN\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | a warm, patient language teacher, clear and unhurried; says every Russian word the way a native Russian speaker would"}
next: {"title":"Russian gender from the last letter: он, она, оно","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/02-russian-gender.cast"}

## Read Russian in 14 letters
sources:
    - id: nkrja
      title: Новый частотный словарь русской лексики (letter frequencies, Russian National Corpus)
      authors: Lyashevskaya & Sharov
      year: 2009
      finding: О Е А И Н Т С Р В К М Д П У together are about 77.6 % of letters in Russian text
    - id: testing
      title: 'Test-enhanced learning: taking memory tests improves long-term retention'
      authors: Roediger & Karpicke
      year: 2006
      finding: Recalling a text beat re-reading it on tests two days and a week later

