    box w_kot2 "КОТ\ncat" #3d3833 say кот height 120 radius 10 icon cat font_size 44 in words1 hidden true
    box w_mama "МАМА\nmum" #3d3833 say мама height 120 radius 10 font_size 44 in words1 hidden true
    box w_tam "ТАМ\nthere" #3d3833 say там height 120 radius 10 font_size 44 in words1 hidden true
    group w_kot_solo members ["w_kot"] fit.h 100 fit.w 250 fit.x 700 fit.y 470 hidden true
    column words1 gap 30 fit.h 410 fit.w 250 fit.x 700 fit.y 190 hidden true
    box w_rest "РЕСТОРАН" #3d3833 say true width 300 height 70 radius 10 font_size 44 hidden true
    box w_rest2 "РЕСТОРАН\nrestaurant" #3d3833 say ресторан width 300 height 120 radius 10 font_size 44 in words2 hidden true
    box w_net "НЕТ\nno" #3d3833 say нет height 120 radius 10 font_size 44 in words2 hidden true
    group w_rest_solo members ["w_rest"] fit.h 100 fit.w 300 fit.x 680 fit.y 440 hidden true
    column words2 gap 80 fit.h 360 fit.w 280 fit.x 690 fit.y 220 hidden true

    card title "Read Russian in 14 letters"

Can you learn to read Russian in a few minutes? Here is the test: by the end, you'll read this.
    draw goal

Most English speakers see this word and read it as "pectopah".
    highlight g1 part РЕСТОРАНЕ

That mistake shows the way in: many of these shapes you already know — and some of them lie.
    fade goal to 0.12

    hide goal

Russian has thirty-three letters, but we'll learn only fourteen of the commonest: together they fill about three letters in every four on a page.
    draw note

We'll go letters, then words, then the text — and you'll test yourself at each step, because pulling a thing from memory fixes it far better than reading it again.
    highlight note

First, five true friends: A, K, M, O and T look and sound just as in English.
    draw row_friends

With only those, try reading a word.
    draw w_kot_solo

    quiz "How does КОТ sound?"
        right: It's кот, kot: every letter a true friend.
        + kot
        * kat
        * kom

    hide w_kot_solo

And кот means cat; мама is mum, and там means there.
    draw w_kot2 w_mama w_tam

    erase words1

Next come the false friends: letters that look English but say something else.
    draw row_liars

В says v, Е says ye, Н says n, Р is a rolled r, С says s, and У says oo.
    blocking false

    highlight t_v duration 0.9

    highlight t_e duration 0.9

    highlight t_n duration 0.9

    highlight t_r duration 1.3

    highlight t_s duration 0.9

    highlight t_u duration 1

Now go back to the word that fooled you.
    draw w_rest_solo

    quiz "How does РЕСТОРАН sound?"
        right: It's ресторан, restoran: a restaurant, once the liars say their real sounds.
        wrong: Р and С are false friends: give them their Russian sounds.
        * pectopah
        + restoran
        * vestoran

    hide w_rest_solo

And this one, which looks like "het", is нет: no.
    draw w_rest2 w_net

    erase words2

Last, three new faces — and a new shape sticks best with a picture or a story attached.
    draw row_new

Д looks like a little house, and it says d, as in дом: house.
    highlight t_d

    box w_dom "ДОМ\nhouse" #3d3833 say дом height 120 radius 10 icon house font_size 44 in words3

И looks like a backwards N; it says ee, and on its own it means "and".
    highlight t_i

П is the Greek pi, and says p, as in суп: soup.
    highlight t_p

    box w_sup "СУП\nsoup" #3d3833 say суп height 120 radius 10 icon ["soup","bowl"] font_size 44 in words3

One more, with a letter from each row: вода, water. Listen: an O without the stress sounds like a.
    box w_voda "ВОДА\nwater" #3d3833 say вода height 120 radius 10 icon ["droplet","water"] font_size 44 in words3
    column words3 gap 30 fit.h 410 fit.w 250 fit.x 700 fit.y 190 hidden true

    ask "Type the word for house." answer ["ДОМ"] keys АКМОТВЕНРСУДИП
        right: дом: house. Д, the little house, then О and М.
        wrong: Start with the little house.

    erase words3

    hide board note

    cards match
        * "КОТ" match cat
        * "ДОМ" match house
        * "СУП" match soup
        * "ВОДА" match water
        * "НЕТ" match no

    ask "Match each Russian word to its meaning." on match store m stage own
        intro: Before the text, pull the words back from memory.
        right: All five, from memory.
        wrong: You got {m} on the first try.

    erase match

    show goal

Now the test from the start, with the letters put away: read it yourself first.
    fade goal to 1 duration 1.2

    quiz "Where is the cat?" pool false
        right: At home: НЕТ, no, then КОТ ДОМА, the cat at home.
        wrong: Find НЕТ in the last line, and the word with Д, the little house.
        * In the restaurant
        + At home
        * With mum

Мама в ресторане: word for word, mum in restaurant; the extra e comes with "in", and Russian needs no "is" and no "the".
    draw g1_en

Там суп и вода: there's soup and water.
    draw g2_en

А кот? Нет, кот дома: and the cat? No, the cat is at home.
    draw g3_en

One honest caveat: this is print, and Russian handwriting looks quite different; that's another small lesson.

So you didn't learn all of Russian: you learned fourteen common letters, leaned on the ones you knew, named the liars, and tested yourself. That was enough to read.
    highlight goal

    quiz "A word you've never seen: how does ТРАНСПОРТ sound?"
        right: It's транспорт, transport: Р, Н and С are the liars, П is pi.
        wrong: Three of its letters are false friends: read them the Russian way.
        * tpahcnopt
        + transport
        * vranstort

And pectopah? It was a restaurant all along. The other nineteen letters fall the same way.
    highlight g1 part РЕСТОРАНЕ effect underline

